{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats","id":1295860,"title":"You died and you are given a choice to being reborn into these splats.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-11T09:58:09-07:00","id":1295860,"title":"You died and you are given a choice to being reborn into these splats.","content":"1. Sin-Eater<br /> 2. Vampire<br /> 3. Changeling<br /> <br /> Which do you choose and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T10:20:17-07:00","id":1295864,"title":"","content":"sin eater I suppose. am actually capable of enjoying my newfound life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T10:48:42-07:00","id":1295871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1295864#post1295864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sin eater I suppose. am actually capable of enjoying my newfound life</div> </div> </div> </div>What obstacles do Vampires, Changelings, and Sin-Eaters have that would detract them from enjoying life? I could be one of these and still have a hedonistic lifestyle, right? I could just make a good effort to stay away from trouble.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T11:59:21-07:00","id":1295888,"title":"","content":"well, vampires are in an uphill battle for their humanity, changeling have to battle for sanity and on the run from the gentry and huntsman, but sin eaters can have a relatively beneficial bargain with the geist and enjoy life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T12:54:05-07:00","id":1295908,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eater. I wanna go help ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T12:59:48-07:00","id":1295911,"title":"","content":"Vampire. Finally a valid excuse to engage in cannibalism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T13:55:39-07:00","id":1295933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1295911#post1295911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire. Finally a valid excuse to engage in cannibalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cannibalism is when the same species consume each other, right? Are you still considered a cannibal since Vampires are a different race. I think you only engage in cannibalism one you are a very old vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T14:15:31-07:00","id":1295936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1295933#post1295933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cannibalism is when the same species consume each other, right? Are you still considered a cannibal since Vampires are a different race. I think you only engage in cannibalism one you are a very old vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Biologically speaking vampires are neither a different species nor a different race. They're humans, just dead and reanimated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T15:41:36-07:00","id":1295956,"title":"","content":"Vampire. Immortality is a big plus, and the social stuff would make it a lot easier. Changelings have too much torment and I can already be a weirdo living for a roughly human lifespan, and I don't want to be hassled by ghosts for the rest of my human life the way a Sin-Eater might. Vampire would probably be the way to go if you don't want to be hassled by people, plus the advantages are pretty wild compared to the drawbacks. Though I'd need to do something about the windows, Dominate would make contract work cheap and easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T17:34:50-07:00","id":1295987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1295956#post1295956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire. Immortality is a big plus, and the social stuff would make it a lot easier. Changelings have too much torment and I can already be a weirdo living for a roughly human lifespan, and I don't want to be hassled by ghosts for the rest of my human life the way a Sin-Eater might. Vampire would probably be the way to go if you don't want to be hassled by people, plus the advantages are pretty wild compared to the drawbacks. Though I'd need to do something about the windows, Dominate would make contract work cheap and easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do ghosts bother a Sin-Eater. I assume they can see and talk to Ghost but they can just ignore them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T17:44:39-07:00","id":1295990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1295987#post1295987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do ghosts bother a Sin-Eater. I assume they can see and talk to Ghost but they can just ignore them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They see and sense sin-eaters, and apparently seek them out to help them do things.<br /> <br /> Imagine if all your neighbors were constantly knocking at your door to try and ask you to help them with stuff. You could ignore the constant knocking and calls for assistance, but it would still be incredibly annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T18:57:08-07:00","id":1296005,"title":"","content":"I dont think ghosts just know a geist when they see one. is there something I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T19:29:11-07:00","id":1296016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1296005#post1296005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont think ghosts just know a geist when they see one. is there something I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bound have something called a Liminal Aura. Their Synergy dictates how large and how powerful it is, but essentially any ghost or Bound within the Aura will recognize you for what you are and you actually create a persistent Manifestation Condition for ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T19:40:06-07:00","id":1296017,"title":"","content":"interesting. I still stand by the bound though,vthey dont have to deal with as many backstabbers as vampires or oaths and the gentry like changelings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T21:12:23-07:00","id":1296033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1296017#post1296017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">interesting. I still stand by the bound though,vthey dont have to deal with as many backstabbers as vampires or oaths and the gentry like changelings</div> </div> </div> </div>An important thing to bear in mind: Unlike the other two splats in this question, Sin-Eaters have almost all of their drawbacks front-loaded.<br /> <br /> Starting vampires have no clan bane, the longest interval for the lowest damage from sunlight, and can sustain themselves on the blood of animals.<br /> <br /> Starting changelings roll a chance die for Clarity damage, have no extra frailties beyond the bane of iron, and can reap Glamour from people with relatively little consequence.<br /> <br /> Starting Sin-Eaters roll a chance die to stop their geist from manifesting in response to their Ban or Bane (or extorting favors out of them to hold it off), haven't yet learned enough about their geist to filter down its less universal trigger for a crisis point, and become automatically detectable to every ghost within a mile (or hemorrhage Willpower to keep from doing so) as soon as they deal with the reason they came back or make headway on figuring out their geist's Whole General Deal, barring the circumstance where they <i>die again</i>.<br /> <br /> The Bound are substantially more task-oriented than the Kindred or the Lost; changelings and vampires can, at least in theory, manage to reach a state of equilibrium where if they leave well enough alone they can last a decade or so without trouble. Changelings and vampires seek power and security because they're desperate and distrustful; Sin-Eaters are <i>haunted</i>, and because of that they have more than just their own concerns to worry about even in the unlikely event that they find a town with no ghosts \u2014 they are, by definition, never alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T22:49:07-07:00","id":1296045,"title":"","content":"Changeling. If a Changeling is patient and clever, he can overcome even his Keeper or the Huntsman sent to recapture him. Furthermore, you can be a frost man with teeth of ice who makes chains out of anything, up to and including cats. Also Hedgespinning items, Goblin Fruits, and meeting cute elven ladies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T08:44:07-07:00","id":1296144,"title":"","content":"sigh. well this got a lot harder. I'll think about it, I'll be posting again later on my new decision (and if I dknt change, I'll explain why)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T20:27:58-07:00","id":1296323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1296144#post1296144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sigh. well this got a lot harder. I'll think about it, I'll be posting again later on my new decision (and if I dknt change, I'll explain why)</div> </div> </div> </div>How did it get harder, Primordial? I assumed this thread was &quot;just for fun&quot;. If you need any help, I'll be glad to brainstorm with ya if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T20:55:31-07:00","id":1296330,"title":"","content":"I'd guess because of the drawbacks to being a Sin-Eater. While they do have a relatively beneficial Bargain with a geist, it's still a burden at times.<br /> <br /> That said they do get a lot of powers, and being able to explore the Underworld pretty much guarantees that even if you grow bored with this world you'll have reasonably easy access to another. They're definitely the choice to go if you want a lot of power over ghosts and mage isn't on the table.<br /> <br /> I'm not a people person at the best of times, so I'd like to avoid the whole geist thing, but some people would enjoy meeting new (dead) people, to the point that I'd be willing to drink the blood of the living (given this hypothetical and fictional example) to avoid it and gain the other vampiric benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-13-2019, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T21:11:00-07:00","id":1296333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1296323#post1296323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How did it get harder, Primordial? I assumed this thread was &amp;quot;just for fun&amp;quot;. If you need any help, I'll be glad to brainstorm with ya if you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>it is just for fun, I just didnt know and wasnt fully aware of the crap sin eaters had to deal with. thanks for offering though!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've decided to stay with Sin eaters. they dont have the vampiric curses, dont live a life that makes them a leech of society and alienate them too much, and while the ghost would DEFINITELY be annoying, there could be some fulfillment in helping them. (I was really close to picking changeling, but the whole being hunted and trusting on the basis of oaths just killed it for me)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T21:50:55-07:00","id":1296339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1296330#post1296330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd guess because of the drawbacks to being a Sin-Eater. While they do have a relatively beneficial Bargain with a geist, it's still a <b>burden</b> at times.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:10px\">I see what you did there.</span><br /> <br /> I'm also in the Vampire boat, pending some new consideration that changes my mind; it facilitates a structure and a routine well enough that one can at least sketch out a plan for the inevitable downward pull of the Blood over time, and the number of angles to keep track of is cut down substantially when you don't have to worry about extradimensional threats as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> That being said, frenzy management is the name of the game as far as Touchstones go night-to-night, and one of the cardinal rules of frenzy management is &quot;stay fed,&quot; so a comfortable unlife relies substantially on getting to grips with the local territories and personalities pretty early on and negotiating a permissive or absent sire. It won't hold up perfectly for a full century, but getting a lease on e.g. all the pets in an apartment complex and a territorial mandate to keep the place tidy is pretty tame compared to a revolving door of unfinished business or trading favors to hide from aliens.<br /> <br /> Then again, if I had any confidence that trauma and Bedlam wouldn't screw me over I'd be a Grim in a heartbeat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-13-2019, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T22:28:06-07:00","id":1296342,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying I wouldn't break in the first few weeks...<br /> <br /> But putting aside the (somewhat disturbing) inherent feeling of resonance with being a Sin-Eater, if I <i>couldn't</i> or <i>didn't try</i> at being one of the Bound, I think something went wrong with my aspirations.<br /> <br /> I feel a little weird saying that as the Changeling Guy, but there it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T09:21:41-07:00","id":1296432,"title":"","content":"Many years ago, Jhonen Vasquez did a comic about a guy obsessed with vampires, to the point of desperately desiring to become one. One night, he gets his opportunity, and jumps on it without hesitance. The twist, though, is that, where the protagonist expected to become some sexy Dracula-type lord of the night, he instead wound up looking more like a more hideous Count Orlock.<br /> <br /> So part of the choice here would depend on how much control one has over the specifics of one's monstrosity. If I were a vampire, I'd hope to be a Daeva or Mekhet rather than Nosferatu (though I'd choose the Nightmares over the Ventrue, to be sure).<br /> <br /> Actually I'd probably not want to be a vampire at all; I can imagine myself too easily beansing up pretty much every aspect of Kindred existence by night five.<br /> <br /> Back in undergrad I used to write some fiction featuring a Sin-Eater who was more or less a self-insert character (I recently read back over some of these stories and they are in retrospect tragicomic). The Bound do have a lot of drawbacks going on, but it must be nice having a clear-cut purpose in life. Plus, maybe your ghost friend is actually really rad if you're lucky.<br /> <br /> Changeling is the Chronicles of Darkness game with which I most identify already, but, as with vampires, wanting to be one of the Lost would depend on how much control I have over what kind of fae I become. If I sign up for that sort of deal while thinking Prince Sidon but getting Rumpelstiltskin, well, that would be a tad irksome. Also in this scenario, does choosing changeling mean having to endure the exquisite tortures of Arcadia? I might have to pass on that, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T10:07:48-07:00","id":1296737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1296033#post1296033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An important thing to bear in mind: Unlike the other two splats in this question, Sin-Eaters have almost all of their drawbacks front-loaded.<br /> <br /> Starting vampires have no clan bane, the longest interval for the lowest damage from sunlight, and can sustain themselves on the blood of animals.<br /> <br /> Starting changelings roll a chance die for Clarity damage, have no extra frailties beyond the bane of iron, and can reap Glamour from people with relatively little consequence.<br /> <br /> Starting Sin-Eaters roll a chance die to stop their geist from manifesting in response to their Ban or Bane (or extorting favors out of them to hold it off), haven't yet learned enough about their geist to filter down its less universal trigger for a crisis point, and become automatically detectable to every ghost within a mile (or hemorrhage Willpower to keep from doing so) as soon as they deal with the reason they came back or make headway on figuring out their geist's Whole General Deal, barring the circumstance where they <i>die again</i>.<br /> <br /> The Bound are substantially more task-oriented than the Kindred or the Lost; changelings and vampires can, at least in theory, manage to reach a state of equilibrium where if they leave well enough alone they can last a decade or so without trouble. Changelings and vampires seek power and security because they're desperate and distrustful; Sin-Eaters are <i>haunted</i>, and because of that they have more than just their own concerns to worry about even in the unlikely event that they find a town with no ghosts \u2014 they are, by definition, never alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Sin-Eater have the worst early-game but their mid to late game is the best out of the three?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T13:09:55-07:00","id":1296779,"title":"","content":"Vampire because it's easiest to go right back to being dead.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eater if I'm actually trying to do something; I wouldn't enjoy being haunted, but it's a pretty minor drawback in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T14:32:21-07:00","id":1296791,"title":"","content":"Beast you get all this cool superpowers . And you can feed on assholes,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T18:05:47-07:00","id":1296849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1296737#post1296737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Sin-Eater have the worst early-game but their mid to late game is the best out of the three?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their most significant means of character advancement is both Trait-agnostic and proportional to the difficulty of their Uncontrolled Bad News state, whereas the narrative widgets the other two lean into for mechanically-sourced drama are measures of attrition and maintenance. Due to Sin-Eaters having a Supernatural Potency Trait that doubles lightly as an Integrity analogue, they have sort of the reverse of Mage and Vampire's &quot;high Humanity/Wisdom for a veteran character means something very different than it does for a beginner.&quot;<br /> <br /> Advancing/completing your geist's Remembrance gets you Synergy and irreversible character advancement that sticks with you even if you lose Synergy, which is important largely because the way Mementos work means many of the incentives to raise your Synergy above 5 (and keep it there) go away \u2014 the baseline Sympathetic relationship combined with a Specific crisis point trigger provides you with a substantial level of control over the outcome of a crisis point without excess complication, but unless you're really serious about having three Touchstones and the capacity for Attributes of 6 or higher it's probably unwise to pump your Liminal Aura strong enough to enable most Manifestations by default, much less to the point where people around you being Claimed is on the table.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that no matter how many Mementos they channel or how much Synergy they cultivate, every Sin-Eater has two things that <i>immediately terminate their main powers</i> \u2014 cold iron is a baneful substance to changelings and blocks their magic contextually, and no amount of Resilience can keep Kindred from taking damage from sunlight altogether, but the Bound have consistent personalized holes in their magical defenses that stay there from rebirth to final death and no amount of resonance with their dark passengers will make those things easier to work around. The timeless semi-immortals generally make trades to get those sorts of vulnerabilities, and they usually don't have to pick up even more to use their higher-end powers.<br /> <br /> &quot;Best&quot; is a bit much, in other words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T07:41:14-07:00","id":1296984,"title":"","content":"Kindred of clan Daeva.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T10:41:17-07:00","id":1297023,"title":"","content":"Very important question: would I be born into the world of the ChroD, or would I be essentially turned into one of the splats in 'our' reality? As in, would I be the only Kindred, or would I have to participate in the Danse, feuds, etc.?<br /> <br /> Currently I'd be torn between Kindred and Sin-Eater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T10:56:38-07:00","id":1297031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1296791#post1296791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast you get all this cool superpowers . And you can feed on assholes,</div> </div> </div> </div>They offered a couple answers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Sin-Eater<br /> 2. Vampire<br /> 3. Changeling<br /> <br /> Which do you choose and why? </div> </div> </div>But I figured they would follow up with other splats later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T11:14:49-07:00","id":1297036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1297023#post1297023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very important question: would I be born into the world of the ChroD, or would I be essentially turned into one of the splats in 'our' reality? As in, would I be the only Kindred, or would I have to participate in the Danse, feuds, etc.?<br /> <br /> Currently I'd be torn between Kindred and Sin-Eater.</div> </div> </div> </div>haven't even thought of that. if our reality, changeling, if ChroD, sin eater","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T11:35:50-07:00","id":1297045,"title":"","content":"I think it's a fairly safe bet that being in the ChroD world is part of the buy-in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T11:39:13-07:00","id":1297047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1295860-you-died-and-you-are-given-a-choice-to-being-reborn-into-these-splats?p=1297045#post1297045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Vi